% Fire.wording — how the facts and changes of Fire.drl read in English.
%
% One line per fluent or event of LPS2's reading of the rule base (the name
% before the colon is the one the reading gives it; the twin's declarations
% list them), then its words, with a place for each of its values, and, if
% wanted, the name LPS knows it by. A line for something the rule base does
% not have is reported and ignored. Without this file the defaults are used:
% `there is an alarm`, `an alarm starts`, `the alarm ends`.

alarm: an alarm is on
alarm_starts: an alarm goes on; known as alarm_goes_on
alarm_ends: the alarm goes off; known as alarm_goes_off
fire_ends: the fire in *a room* is put out; known as fire_is_put_out
